# {{ .Name }} ({{ .Type | title }})

Get information on a local domain linked to an application, by `application_id` and
`domain_name`.

## Example Usage

```terraform
data "wallix-bastion_application" "web_server" {
  application_name = "web_server"
}

# Get information about a specific local domain of this application
data "wallix-bastion_application_localdomain" "web_local" {
  application_id = data.wallix-bastion_application.web_server.id
  domain_name     = "local"
}

# Use the local domain in an account lookup
data "wallix-bastion_application_localdomain_account" "web_admin" {
  application_id = data.wallix-bastion_application.web_server.id
  domain_id       = data.wallix-bastion_application_localdomain.web_local.id
  account_name    = "web_administrator"
}

# Check whether password change is enabled on this local domain
output "web_local_password_change_enabled" {
  value = data.wallix-bastion_application_localdomain.web_local.enable_password_change
}
```

{{ .SchemaMarkdown | trimspace }}

## Usage Notes

### Lookup Keys

Both `application_id` (the parent application's ID) and `domain_name` are required to identify
the local domain. The data source returns an error if no local domain with that name exists on
the given application.

### Password Management

- **enable_password_change**: Whether password changes are enabled for accounts in this domain
- **password_change_policy**: The password policy associated with password changes
- **password_change_plugin**: The plugin used to perform password changes
- **password_change_plugin_parameters**: Plugin-specific parameters; marked sensitive since it
  may contain connection details for the target application

### Using the Result

The data source's `id` (the local domain's ID) is the value to pass as `domain_id` when reading
or managing `wallix-bastion_application_localdomain_account` resources scoped to this domain.
